      "message": "`config.js:3` holds `SESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30`, read by `server.js` as the session expiry. The edit is one value, but it's a security-posture change, so I want your confirmation before making it.\n\nConsequence: going 30m → 480m (8h) means a stolen or abandoned session stays valid for 16× longer. On a shared or unattended machine, a walked-away-from browser stays authenticated for a full workday, and a leaked session token gives an attacker an 8-hour window instead of 30 minutes. There's no idle-vs-absolute distinction in this config — it's a single flat timeout — so this extends the window even for sessions with no activity.\n\nConfirm and I'll set it to `SESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 480`, nothing else.",
